---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import Term from '../../components/journey/Term.astro';
import LessonRef from '../../components/journey/LessonRef.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';

const ids = ['claims.hosting.cloudflareStatic', 'claims.hosting.cloudflarePaid', 'claims.hosting.githubPagesPublic'];
---
<Journey chapter="stack" first="commit" title="Git, GitHub and hosting" description="A commit is a save point you can go back to, GitHub keeps a copy online, a pull request holds a change until it is checked, and a site is hosted as finished pages or as a server with a database.">
  <Step id="commit" title="A commit is a save point">
    <p>The coding agent from <LessonRef id="ai" step="modes" /> edits the files of <Term id="project" />. Save a version first with a <Term id="commit" />, let it break something, then ask for the old one back.</p>
    <div class="pick" role="group" aria-label="Saved before the change?">
      <button type="button" data-do="saved" data-val="yes" data-default aria-pressed="true">Saved first</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="saved" data-val="no" aria-pressed="false">Not saved</button>
    </div>
    <ForLevel is="plain"><p>You do not type these yourself: “Save this version with Git” is enough.</p></ForLevel>
    <More title="The commands" level="technical">
      <pre><code>git init                          # once, in the folder
git add -A
git commit -m "Member list works"
git status                        # what changed since
git restore .                     # throw those changes away</code></pre>
    </More>
  </Step>

  <Step id="github" title="GitHub keeps a copy online">
    <p>Pushing sends your commits to GitHub, a website that keeps a copy of your project. Then the laptop is left on a train.</p>
    <div class="pick" role="group" aria-label="Pushed to GitHub?">
      <button type="button" data-do="pushed" data-val="yes" data-default aria-pressed="true">Pushed</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="pushed" data-val="no" aria-pressed="false">Never pushed</button>
    </div>
    <More title="The commands" level="technical">
      <pre><code># origin is the name for the copy on GitHub
git remote add origin https://github.com/you/club-list.git
git push -u origin main           # first time
git push                          # after that
git clone https://github.com/you/club-list.git   # on the new laptop</code></pre>
    </More>
  </Step>

  <Step id="branch" title="A branch, and a pull request">
    <p><Term id="main" /> is the version people use. A <Term id="branch" /> is a line of work beside it, and a <Term id="pull-request" /> asks to bring it into main once the check has run and you have looked.</p>
    <div class="pick" role="group" aria-label="Where the change goes">
      <button type="button" data-do="branch" data-val="no" aria-pressed="false">Straight to main</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="branch" data-val="yes" data-default aria-pressed="true">On a branch</button>
    </div>
    <More title="The commands" level="technical">
      <pre><code>git switch -c paid-date           # a new branch
git push -u origin paid-date      # then “Compare &amp; pull request” on GitHub
git switch main &amp;&amp; git merge paid-date   # or the Merge button</code></pre>
      <p>The check on a pull request is usually CI (continuous integration): a GitHub Actions workflow that runs <code>npm test</code> on every push.</p>
    </More>
  </Step>

  <Step id="hosting" title="Finished pages, or a server">
    <p>Static hosting hands out finished pages; a server runs your code and keeps a database. The coach marks Sam as paid: does the treasurer see it?</p>
    <div class="pick" role="group" aria-label="How it is hosted">
      <button type="button" data-do="host" data-val="static" data-default aria-pressed="true">Static</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="host" data-val="dynamic" aria-pressed="false">Server and database</button>
    </div>
    <More title="What it costs">
      <p><Fact id="claims.hosting.cloudflareStatic" show="claim" /> <Fact id="claims.hosting.cloudflarePaid" show="claim" /> <Fact id="claims.hosting.githubPagesPublic" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
    <More title="Choosing between them" level="engineer">
        <dl class="j-defs">
          <dt>Static</dt><dd>No runtime to patch, no secrets on a server. Shared state needs a hosted service behind it.</dd>
          <dt>Server</dt><dd>One source of truth and server-side checks on who may change what. You now own uptime, backups, secrets and upgrades.</dd>
          <dt>Between them</dt><dd>Static pages plus small functions and a managed database: little to run, but each piece is one more account and one more bill.</dd>
        </dl>
    </More>
  </Step>

  <Step id="specs" title="How big a server">
    <p>A rented server comes in sizes: processor cores, memory and disk, together called its specs. Grow the club and watch the smallest one.</p>
    <div class="control">
      <label for="members">Members</label>
      <input id="members" type="range" min="0" max="3" step="1" value="0" data-bind="members" aria-label="Club members" aria-valuetext="40 members" />
    </div>
    <Next from="stack" more={[{ href: 'wiki/version-control/', text: 'Version control', side: true }, { href: 'wiki/deployment/', text: 'Deployment', side: true }, { href: 'wiki/database/', text: 'Database', side: true }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The club, its members, the visits per member and the server's capacity are made up. The commands were run once in a test repository.</p>
    <Verified ids={ids} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
